r":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/github-linguist/linguist/cfd7a0113aa1efab99faeff38756f0ed4d48add8/lib/linguist/languages.yml","matched":true,"sha256":"05e20bd736808a9e468ae1546e1a3b518b95fa215ee6f746903f7e164a9fd37b","started_utc":"2026-11-23T14:32:49.672+00:00","status":200}],"scirs_sha256":"08a628a92932cf83532df3788d4a579d1b2158b058fd94c90266fb9f297187f6","source_commit":"5d16988f5300397caa0c1a660a3fba6b26948c5b","specimen_findings":{"myobject.sql":"Contains CREATE TYPE object and table-type definitions, member signatures and AUTHID, then uses SQL*Plus slash and PROMPT. It is an object-DDL and client-command control rather than a stand-alone procedural block.","packagebody.pkb":"Contains a package body, procedural subprogram definitions and a SQL query used by a cursor. The trailing slash has client scope.","packageheader.pks":"Contains a package specification, constant and procedure and function declarations. The trailing slash has client scope.","plsqlguide.pck":"Contains a package specification and body, a procedural loop over an embedded SQL query, and HTML/JavaScript inside text literals rather than the procedural grammar.","prime#.plsql":"Contains package specification and body, an associative array, subprograms, control flow and exception raising. The trailing slash has client scope.","print_bool.prc":"Contains a procedure, formal mode and defaults, and a procedural body with an expression and database package call.","videodb.ddl":"Contains two Oracle SQL CREATE TABLE statements and one PL/SQL procedure with bulk collection, typed local declarations and a for-loop. Slashes are client commands.","who_called_me.sql":"Contains procedure syntax with OUT modes, local declarations and a procedural loop. Its .sql extension does not identify the language alone."}}}
